# Simple code first

- Write code a human intern can type from memory. Short files. Short functions.
- No big logic. One function does one small step.
- Do not add mixins stacks, services, managers, or extra apps unless the user asks.
- Prefer copy-paste Django patterns: `ModelForm` with `Meta`, `admin.site.register`, simple `if` in views.
- If a feature needs more than ~30 lines of logic, split it into two small functions — do not nest classes.

```python
# BAD — hard to type, extra layers
class EnrollmentService:
    def complete_and_unlock(self, user, course):
        ...

# GOOD — plain steps
if enrollment.status == "assigned":
    enrollment.status = "completed"
    enrollment.save()
```
